---
// src/components/ui/HeroDotPattern.astro
// Purely decorative dot-matrix texture for the hero's left/right blank
// margins (the empty bg-electric space beside the centered max-w-2xl
// text column). Inspired by inertiajs.com's hero: soft, organic-looking
// clusters of small dots rather than a literal shape (no clouds/logos).
//
// This is a NEW, separate decorative layer from HeroScatterDecoration.astro
// — that component was built for a light hero background (frosted-glass
// panels tinted with signal colors) and doesn't apply to Hero.astro's
// current solid `bg-electric` dark background. This file reuses only its
// conventions (see below), not its markup or colors.
//
// COLOR: white only, opacity in the ~18-24% range — clearly noticeable
// as a texture against bg-electric (#3B4EFF) without competing with the
// content column. (Bumped up from an earlier, too-subtle ~10-15% pass.)
// No new color tokens introduced.
//
// VISIBILITY: like HeroScatterDecoration.astro, the `lg:`-only visibility
// toggle is NOT hardcoded in this file — the consumer (Hero.astro) applies
// `class="hidden lg:block"` on this component's usage, which flows into
// the `class` prop below and lands on the wrapper.
//
// TEXT-COLUMN CLEARANCE: Hero.astro centers its content in a `max-w-2xl`
// (672px) column with no max-width on the `<section>` itself. At the
// narrowest width this component ever renders (`lg:` = 1024px), that
// column spans roughly 17%-83% of the viewport. Every cluster below —
// on both sides — sits within the outer ~-4% to ~20% margin on its
// respective side (left-side clusters hug the left edge, right-side
// clusters hug the right edge), and each cluster's dot-visible area is
// itself faded out via a radial mask well before its bounding box's
// inner edge — so the effective dot texture clears the column with room
// to spare at 1024px and only gains clearance as the viewport widens
// further. Only the horizontal placement is constrained this way; the
// clusters are free to vary vertically (see "COVERAGE" below) since the
// text column's clearance is purely a left/right concern.
//
// COVERAGE: four clusters per side (eight total), staggered across the
// section's full height — not just the two original corners — so the
// texture reads continuously from top to bottom on both margins. Sizes
// and opacities are varied per cluster (see markup) for a natural,
// non-repetitive scatter rather than a uniform repeated tile.
//
// STACKING ORDER: positioned at `-z-[5]`, matching HeroScatterDecoration's
// documented reasoning — less negative than the `.hero-grain` overlay's
// `-z-[9]` (grain paints furthest back, this dot texture paints just in
// front of it), while still sitting behind the in-flow, un-z-indexed
// content column.
//
// Asymmetric-but-balanced layout: four clusters per side, alternating
// varied sizes and opacities top-to-bottom, same composition idea as the
// reference (inertiajs.com) — organic and scattered, not a literal copy
// and not a uniform grid.
//
// Implementation: CSS `radial-gradient` for the repeating dot grid, with
// a second radial-gradient used as a `mask-image` so each cluster fades
// out into the background at its edges (organic blob silhouette) instead
// of reading as a hard-edged rectangle of dots. No inline `style="..."`
// attributes anywhere below; the <style> block only carries the
// background-image/mask-image pattern itself, which has no Tailwind
// utility equivalent. All sizing/position/opacity is Tailwind classes.

export interface Props {
  class?: string;
}

const { class: className } = Astro.props;
---

<div
  class:list={['pointer-events-none absolute -z-[5] inset-0', className]}
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  <!-- Left side, top-to-bottom. -->
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute top-[4%] left-[-4%] h-64 w-64 opacity-20"></div>
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute top-[28%] left-[-2%] h-52 w-52 opacity-[0.18]"></div>
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute bottom-[28%] left-[-3%] h-72 w-72 opacity-[0.22]"></div>
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute bottom-[4%] left-[-2%] h-60 w-60 opacity-20"></div>

  <!-- Right side, top-to-bottom — mirrored, varied sizes/opacities so it
       doesn't read as a literal duplicate of the left column. -->
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute top-[8%] right-[-3%] h-60 w-60 opacity-[0.19]"></div>
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute top-[32%] right-[-4%] h-80 w-80 opacity-[0.24]"></div>
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute bottom-[24%] right-[-2%] h-56 w-56 opacity-[0.18]"></div>
  <div class="hero-dot-cluster absolute bottom-[2%] right-[-3%] h-64 w-64 opacity-[0.22]"></div>
</div>

<style>
  /* Small repeating white dots, softened at the edges by a radial mask
     so the cluster reads as an organic blob rather than a dot-filled
     rectangle. Dot color is fully opaque white; the ~18-24% opacity
     comes from each cluster div's Tailwind opacity-* utility above, so
     there's a single source of truth for the "how visible" knob. */
  .hero-dot-cluster {
    background-image: radial-gradient(circle, #fff 1px, transparent 1.6px);
    background-size: 14px 14px;
    -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 55% at 50% 50%, #000 0%, #000 35%, transparent 72%);
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 55% 55% at 50% 50%, #000 0%, #000 35%, transparent 72%);
  }
</style>
